    "approvedArt": "docs/visuals/20261122_shen_shang_turnaround/Head.png",
    "workflow": "Front and profile control the anatomy. The 35 degree image serves as holdout. Each eyeball is a separate closed manifold, with native sclera, limbus, iris, pupil and pigment vertices. The 3072-pixel skin, roughness and relief atlases are packed. The scalp, brow and facial hair are supplied by the separate grooming source. Editable closed wet eyelid margins, medial canthi and tapered eyelashes have been added. The alar walls, rounded columella, central upper-lip tubercle and lower vermilion have been sculpted against the latest portrait. A packed fourth data image carries curved vermilion relief, under-eye folds, roughness modulation and a localized tissue mask. A reversible shape key closes the original lips through continuous local deformation. A second reversible key, Auricle and submandibular sculpt, shapes the bilateral cartilage and lobules, malar transition, underside of the jaw and neck. It is active at 1.0. Two subsequent native shape keys adjust the palpebral arc and roll, malar projection, nasal-adjacent and buccal tissue, zygomatic arch and masseter under the approved facial landmarks. The packed sRGB albedo reduces residual broad photographic shading in the cheeks. A further native key shapes the posterior oblique arch, buccal hollow and broad masseter. A corrected packed albedo feathers the two photographic transition edges and supplies fine skin variation in the lateral jaw and neck. Selected eye-only G5c reshapes the upper and lower lid arcs and the temporal commissure. The temporal scleral wall sits beneath the modeled lids and the medial lacrimal tissue thins into the lid edge. The central iris, pupil, and eye object transforms are preserved."
  },
